  "question": "Background / Context\n\nThe \"Great Outdoors\" (GO) is a fictitious outdoor equipment retail chain. It manages data related to daily sales, methods, retailers, and products through the GO Sales dataset provided by IBM. The dataset includes detailed information on how sales transactions are processed within the retail chain.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe primary goal of the project is to develop a predictive model that estimates the sale quantity of products within the GO retail chain. This model will enable stakeholders to optimize inventory and improve sales strategies by anticipating demand more accurately.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n1. Data Analysts: Responsible for analyzing sales data and developing predictive models.\n2. Retail Managers: Use insights from the predictive model to adjust inventory levels and enhance sales performance.\n3. Business Strategists: Utilize the predictive data to inform broader business decisions and strategies.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Data Integration: Collect and integrate sales data from existing database tables (`go_1k`, `go_daily_sales`, `go_methods`, `go_products`, `go_retailers`).\n2. Sales Prediction: Develop and implement predictive algorithms to forecast the quantity of sales based on historical data.\n3. Reporting: Generate reports and visualizations to display predicted sales quantities and trends.\n4. User Interface: Design an interface that allows users to easily access and interpret the predictions and reports.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Performance: The system should process the data and generate predictions within a reasonable timeframe to support continuous decision-making.\n2. Scalability: Ensure that the system can handle increased data volume and complexity as the business grows.\n3. Security: Protect sensitive sales and product data from unauthorized access or exposure.\n4. Usability: Design the user interface to be intuitive and accessible to users with varying levels of technical expertise.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0109\nCREATE TABLE `go_methods` (\n  `method_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `method_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`method_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `go_products` (\n  `product_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `product_line` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `product_type` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `go_retailers` (\n  `retailer_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `retailer_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `retailer_type` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`retailer_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `go_1k` (\n  `sale_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sale_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `retailer_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `product_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `method_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `sale_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sale_amount` decimal(12,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sale_id`),\n  KEY `go_1k_ibfk_1` (`retailer_code`),\n  KEY `go_1k_ibfk_2` (`product_code`),\n  KEY `go_1k_ibfk_3` (`method_code`),\n  CONSTRAINT `go_1k_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`retailer_code`) REFERENCES `go_retailers` (`retailer_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `go_1k_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_code`) REFERENCES `go_products` (`product_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `go_1k_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`method_code`) REFERENCES `go_methods` (`method_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `go_daily_sales` (\n  `daily_sales_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sale_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `product_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `retailer_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `method_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `total_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `total_amount` decimal(12,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`daily_sales_id`),\n  KEY `go_daily_sales_ibfk_1` (`product_code`),\n  KEY `go_daily_sales_ibfk_2` (`retailer_code`),\n  KEY `go_daily_sales_ibfk_3` (`method_code`),\n  CONSTRAINT `go_daily_sales_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`product_code`) REFERENCES `go_products` (`product_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `go_daily_sales_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`retailer_code`) REFERENCES `go_retailers` (`retailer_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `go_daily_sales_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`method_code`) REFERENCES `go_methods` (`method_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
